<title>SOUTH KOREA: Daewoo Corp wins Nigeria LNG plant deal.</title>
<headline>Daewoo Corp wins Nigeria LNG plant deal.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Daewoo Corp said on Tuesday it had won a $48 million order as part of a project to build a huge liquefied natural gas (LNG) plant in Nigeria.</p>
<p>The $2.2 billion project has been promoted by a consortium between France's Technip SA, Italy's Snamprogetti, Britain's M W Kellogg and Japan's JGC Corp, a Daewoo statement said.</p>
<p>The Daewoo Group  unit said it was almost sure to be awarded two more orders, valued at a combined $148 million.</p>
<p>But it did not give further details.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
